  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice.\r\rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\rOS Map & Block Plan P099 Rev A 07/11/2025; Site Plan 360-100 May 2015; Block Plan (Existing) May 2015 360-101 May 2015; Floor Plans (Existing) May 2015 360-102 May 2015; Elevations (Existing) May 2015 360-104 May 2015; Sections (Existing) May 2015 360-105 May 2015; Roof Plan (Existing) May 2015 360-103 May 2015; Block Plan (Proposed) P100 RevA 07/11/2025; Proposed Drawings  P101 Rev A 07/11/2025; Proposed Drawings P102 Rev A 07/11/2025; Highway Safety Impact Form; Planning, Design and Access Statement; SuDS Pro Forma Sheet; Flood Risk Assessment; Fire Statement.\r\r Reason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied by more than seven residents at any one time without first obtaining the approval, in writing, of the Local Planning Authority. \r\rReason: To ensure that the future occupation of the building does not adversely affect the adjoining premises/immediate.\r",
    "No independent laundry facilities shall be installed within any of the bedrooms. With the exception of Bedroom 7, no independent cooking facilities shall be provided within any of the bedrooms. The communal kitchen and dining/living rooms shall be retained in perpetuity.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "Cycle parking, as indicated on drawing \"Proposed Drawings Plan P101 RevA dated 07 November 2025\", shall be provided within in accordance with the following requirements:\r\ro Provision of a minimum of SEVEN long stay cycle parking spaces.\r\ro in an accessible location: the access route to the long stay store should be a minimum of 1.2m wide to enable the bike to enter the store, should be step free and involve no more than 2 doors or gates (excluding the store door) which must also have a minimum opening width of 1.2m;\r\ro secured: with a British Standard mortice lock or access fob;\r\ro fully enclosed: 4 walls and a roof.\r\ro the front boundary wall and gate shall not exceed 1m in height.\r\rReason: To ensure the provision of accessible, secure, and adequate cycle parking facilities and to safeguard the character and appearance of the area.\r",
    "All new external work shall be carried out in materials that resemble, as closely as possible, in colour and texture as specified in the approved application. \r \rReason: To safeguard the appearance of the premises and the character of the immediate area.\r",
    "All new external work shall be carried out in materials that resemble, as closely as possible, in colour and texture as specified in the approved application. \r \rReason: To safeguard the appearance of the premises and the character of the immediate area.\r"
  ],
